id: decisions/016-migration-mode
title: "Complete sweep or migrate-on-touch, per field"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'migration-completeness'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: migration-completeness
axis_gloss: "whether a rename or vocabulary change is carried through every affected artifact, or only where it was convenient"
poles:
  a: partial-migration
  b: complete-migration
split: leaning
draft_status: full
leverage: 14.7
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(14) x split_weight(0.7) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.5)"

question: >
  When a rule changes, must every affected record be carried across at once, or
  may records drift until their author next touches them?

why_it_matters: >
  The extension rename was carried through completely with a fail-closed
  validator, while the epistemic-status fix touched one template comment and
  left ~85 records to migrate 'never in bulk', and four contracts still read
  2026-07-01 after their index nodes moved on. Once answered, a bot that finds a
  drifted record knows whether to fix it, ledger it, or leave it, and a child
  Yawn knows whether the rule it inherits is already true of its parent's
  records.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    12 judgments sit at partial-migration (1 authored) and 2 at complete-migration
    (2 authored). The repository asserts both directions on this axis.
  attributed_to: TAXONOMY.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether 'never in bulk' in
    records/epistemic-status-drift-ledger-2026-08-28.yawn is a principle
    (authorship and history are not overwritten) or a resource constraint at the
    time.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      rule: Migrations are opportunistic. A record migrates when its author next
      touches it, never in bulk. A drift ledger in records/ names the debt and a
      test holds a frozen grandfather list that may only shrink.
    cost: "Drifted records stay drifted indefinitely; every consumer must tolerate both old and new form."
    risk: "Records nobody touches never migrate, and the ledger becomes the permanent state."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "For each migration, a test modelled on tests/epistemic-status-vocabulary.test.mjs with a frozen grandfather map."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0071"
      - "J0347"
      - "J0388"
      - "J0451"
      - "J0593"
      - "J0626"
  - name: B
    description: >
      rule: Migrations are complete. A rule change lands with every affected record
      updated in the same change, and a validator in scripts/ fails on any
      straggler, as migrations/2026-08-17-canonical-extension.yawn did.
    cost: "Bulk rewrites of ~85 records for epistemic status alone; authorship of those records is overwritten by the migrator."
    risk: "Contradicts the authored 'never in bulk' rule (J0593) and the repo's stance that history is not rewritten silently."
    reversibility: false
    proof_needed: "A validator in npm run validate per migration with zero grandfather list."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0288"
      - "J0745"
  - name: C
    description: >
      rule: Every migration receipt in migrations/ declares its mode. Fields a
      validator can check (extension, epistemic_status, status enum, hash format,
      schemaVersion) migrate completely or with a frozen grandfather list that may
      only shrink, enforced by a test. Prose, dates and proof.source lists migrate
      on touch, and the receipt names the ledger that tracks them.
    cost: "One field (mode) and one pointer (ledger) added to migrations/node.yawn rules and to each receipt; the J0347 contracts and interface/move.yawn are either updated or ledgered."
    risk: "Everything hard is declared prose and migrated on touch, so mode becomes a label for avoiding work."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Extend migrations/node.yawn rules to require mode and ledger; a test in tests/ that every receipt in migrations/ carries mode: complete|opportunistic and that opportunistic ones name a test holding a grandfather list."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0288"
      - "J0745"
      - "J0593"
      - "J0626"

recommendation:
  option_ref: C
  confidence: 0.75
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    Both poles are authored, for two different migrations: the extension rename
    (J0288, J0745, contract-defined and proof-attached) was complete and
    fail-closed; the epistemic-status containment (J0593, J0626, outcome-attached)
    was deliberately opportunistic and forbids bulk. The revealed partials (J0347,
    J0388, J0451) are unledgered drift with no receipt. The repo's most
    proof-attached practice is already the hybrid:
    tests/epistemic-status-vocabulary.test.mjs enforces going forward and
    grandfathers by name with a ledger that may only shrink (GROUND_TRUTH FACT 7).
    C makes that hybrid the stated rule and requires each receipt to say which
    mode it is in.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "migrations/node.yawn rules require every migration receipt to declare mode: complete or opportunistic and, if opportunistic, to name its ledger test."
    - "Every opportunistic migration has a test in tests/ with a frozen grandfather list that may only shrink, and the suite passes."
    - "database/feedback-intake.yawn, feedback/codex-t4o-parser.yawn, feedback/email-intake.yawn, feedback/form.yawn and interface/move.yawn are either updated or named in a ledger."

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A migration receipt says complete but a grep within its own declared scope
    finds untouched records.
  status: proposed

evidence_sample:
  - "J0071"
  - "J0347"
  - "J0388"
  - "J0451"
  - "J0593"
  - "J0626"
  - "J0288"
  - "J0745"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
  id_index: TAXONOMY.md
